Just a note to non-Finnish readers, most of those are first or family
names for modern Finns; those for r are mostly politicians or some
celebrities.  Those Ts have celebrities' first names as well...
Archeologists have more 'traditional' Finnish names -- of course, some
are so common that many celebrities would have it as their name.  All
the As are male names, by the way, whereas only 'Karita' is a female
name of them all. 

And isn't there something about that you couldn't use hyphens in a
character's name?

            * * *

If you want to use 'real' names from the Finnish national epoch,
Kalevala, and old myths you could use the following (without dotted
letters): 

Kaleva, Vainamoinen (a sage/bard), Ilmarinen (a smith, epiteth 'Seppo'),
Lemminkainen, Antero, Joukahainen, Ukko (really the main god), Tapio
(god of forest), Pekko, Pellervo, Sampsa, Ahti (spirit in the sea),
Iku-Turso (a sea monster...)

There are a few female names as well: Ilmatar, Aino, Louhi (perhaps
chaotic, turned herself into a bird), Maria/Marja (the latter form
means "berry").

